{"id": "EUVD-2026-103800", "enisaUuid": "8afc0c57-4920-312d-93b2-985986f8a48e", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nHID: bpf: cast size to ssize_t when checking hid_bpf_hw_request\n\nAs reported by Sashiko:\nIf a transport driver encounters a hardware error and returns a negative\nerror code such as -EPIPE, ret is implicitly promoted to size_t when\ncompared against size. This causes the negative error code to evaluate\nas a large positive number, making the (ret > size) condition true.\n\nThis silently converts the hardware error into a success return value\nand copies the unmodified buffer back, which could leave BPF programs\noperating on uninitialized or stale data.\n\nFix this by casting size into ssize_t to return the actual negative\nerror code.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:51:21", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:26:54", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8b85ef0f561039e249c3f883c5280a1449c6dbee", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/97be6396817bd3b11d06239010d27902940bfaa9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f9f808227554b2c116fd07dd2328ecd74ea3f411", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3afefbfe55c2a8a0c4bdf6f4cc1f773da120027c"], "aliases": ["GHSA-243p-r44x-jh77", "CVE-2026-98860"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "029c031f-57ef-3b1c-8159-eb25bb527ad4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "eb57dae20fdf6f3069cdc07821fa3bb46de381d7"}, {"id": "0dcb5936-f081-3cc3-a09e-c91868f218ce", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "1eda9b6d-016c-331d-9ce8-bfdb1845a1a2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "24a33cc8-96cc-301d-99e8-032ac7d68115", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d6efaa50af62fb0790dd1fd4e7e5506b46312510 <8b85ef0f561039e249c3f883c5280a1449c6dbee"}, {"id": "2cd9641f-f01a-3eb1-b925-445f4416aaf0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "75d08d1a-6532-312b-90e2-7cf7b2a7bdfb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12.78 <6.12.113"}, {"id": "9b7b1d45-d60c-37de-b59c-7e11a3b030bf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2b658c1c442ec1cd9eec5ead98d68662c40fe645 <f9f808227554b2c116fd07dd2328ecd74ea3f411"}, {"id": "9c702716-fe76-3ad8-a4e8-480c5a96f1aa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2b658c1c442ec1cd9eec5ead98d68662c40fe645 <3afefbfe55c2a8a0c4bdf6f4cc1f773da120027c"}, {"id": "b06bd693-f762-3a63-a66a-f3d7761eb084", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "cefd7c31-5f86-3d06-a2b1-140eee95c812", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.19.10 <6.20"}, {"id": "d6fadaf4-0444-3139-ada9-a05c781de709", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "df119da7-033a-33b3-9bcd-8f6cffcc44f1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18.20 <6.18.56"}, {"id": "f73905b3-e57a-3348-aeb1-0636b227bb77", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.0"}, {"id": "ff6e1771-26fe-3c68-b200-6c2a072901b2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "73c5b5aea1c443239c8cb4191b4af7a4bd6fd7b1 <97be6396817bd3b11d06239010d27902940bfaa9"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0a9e68f7-46af-35a4-871d-240594e9bf0b", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}